<%# The team is chosen once here, rather than named on every line the way
    upstream does. The reader may manage some teams and not others, and a team
    name typed into a line could name one they do not — a scope this page can
    only enforce on a value it drew the choices for itself.

    Rendered above the action select because it is the first thing the reader
    has to decide, and because the pasted list below means nothing without it. %>

<%# Inactive teams are still offered — a team stood down for the season can
    still need its history filled in — but the label says which, because picking
    one by mistake leaves no trace on any roster afterwards. %>
<% choices = manageable_teams.map { |team| [title_marking_inactive(team), team.id] } %>

<%# to_s rather than to_i: a param can arrive array- or hash-shaped, and neither
    answers to_i. Anything that is not a plain id simply selects nothing. %>
<%= f.select :team_id,
             options_for_select(choices, params[:team_id].to_s),
             { label: "Team", required: true, prompt: "Choose a team",
               help_text: "Listing the teams you may record history for." },
             { class: "w-full sm:w-96" } %>
